# The enlargement sieve: established geometry and outstanding intrinsic cases

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, 16.3.9–11,
printed pp.1180–1181 / PDF pp.1197–1198.

The exports prove the two-rank bounds for the actual layer closure K,
the odd-rank nonfusion implication, and both Sylow centralizer conclusions
under the exact earlier uniform shape and proper component outputs.
The four source alternatives and the compatible marking of K⟨z⟩, K, L,
and z inside S₈ are specified in Contracts.

The intrinsic rank sieve must still eliminate swapped components and the
excluded quasisimple families, provide the odd-rank bounds, and reduce to
the four alternatives. The local conjugacy t ∼ tz, the order-four lift
obstruction and the remaining sporadic-cover exclusions are also required.
Finally the surviving binary graph-action case must construct the single
MarkedEightSix equivalence. Accordingly this module does not yet assert
the completed numbered results 16.3.9–11 or their final marked conclusion.
-/
